          "text": "Clinical Indication  \nHistory of drug-responsive focal epilepsy with focal-to-bilateral tonic-clonic seizures beginning at age 61 and occurring five times per week. Genetic etiology attributed to the causative SCN1A variant c.5734C>T. Current antiseizure medication is zonisamide.\n\nTechnique  \nRoutine scalp EEG recording performed using standard electrode placement and reviewed in referential and bipolar montages.\n\nFindings  \nSpecific background, interictal, and ictal EEG findings were not provided; therefore, no electrographic abnormalities are asserted.\n\nImpression  \nThe routine EEG cannot be further interpreted without documented electrographic findings. The reported epilepsy and seizure classifications are based on the clinical history and not inferred from this EEG.",
